<h2 id="implementation" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4">Part III: The Implementation</h2>

<h3 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">3.1 The Eight-Layer Defense Stack</h3>

<p class="text-base text-brand-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
  Every agent action passes through a layered pipeline. Layers are cumulative — a request must clear each
  gate in order:
</p>

<ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-base text-brand-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2">
  <li><strong>Input Sanitization</strong> — prompt injection filtering, constraint persistence outside the context window</li>
  <li><strong>Permission Check</strong> — per-tool explicit grants under per-agent Ed25519 identity</li>
  <li><strong>Policy Decision Tree</strong> — GOA autonomy tier classification; rule → mode → SafetyGate → human</li>
  <li><strong>Sandbox Isolation</strong> — untrusted tool and code execution in containment</li>
  <li><strong>SafetyGate</strong> — 19-class threat assessment with weighted scoring</li>
  <li><strong>Policy Decision (Layer 6)</strong> — final allow/deny with human-in-the-loop escalation (~3%)</li>
  <li><strong>Circuit Breaker</strong> — 3 consecutive failures → HALT absorbing state, 30s cooldown</li>
  <li><strong>Telemetry &amp; Audit</strong> — Merkle-aggregated, Ed25519-signed, tamper-evident audit chain</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">3.2 Five-Line Integration (maref_lite)</h3>

<p class="text-base text-brand-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
  The governance overlay requires no changes to existing agent logic:
</p>

<pre class="bg-surface-trench p-4 rounded text-sm text-brand-text-secondary overflow-x-auto mb-6"><code>
from maref_lite.governance import GovernanceOverlay
from maref_lite.state_machine import GovernanceState

overlay = GovernanceOverlay()                  # 1. attach to any framework
overlay._state_machine.transition(GovernanceState.OBSERVE)   # 2.
overlay._state_machine.transition(GovernanceState.ANALYZE)   # 3.
print(overlay.get_status())                    # 4.
# route tool calls through overlay.check(call) — 5.
</code></pre>

<p class="text-base text-brand-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
  MAREF is framework-agnostic by construction: it implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP, six
  transport types) and Google A2A v0.3, with production adapters for AutoGen, CrewAI, LangGraph, Dify,
  and Coze. As a result, integration typically completes in under an hour.
</p>

<h3 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">3.3 Cryptographic Audit Chain</h3>

<p class="text-base text-brand-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
  Every governance decision is recorded in a Merkle-aggregated audit chain: SHA-3 for hashing, Ed25519
  per-agent signatures for non-repudiation, and optional Chinese national cryptography (SM2/SM3/SM4-GCM,
  GB/T 32918) for organizations operating under PRC compliance requirements. Critically, the Merkle root
  makes the log tamper-evident — any post-hoc deletion or edit invalidates all subsequent hashes, and
  federation allows cross-organization root comparison.
</p>

